TriXium PCIe drivers (derived from LitePCIe's)

  trixium.ko    /dev/trixiumN: BAR0 (CSRs, the weight loader) and the DMA rings.
  liteuart.ko   /dev/ttyLXUN: the firmware console over PCIe (the crossover UART).

csr.h, soc.h and mem.h are generated per SoC build and must come from the build whose
bitstream is on the card: the build scripts generate them (--driver) in
build/<name>/driver/kernel/ and the bring-up scripts copy them here.

- Build both modules:

  make

- Load both modules and make the device nodes world-writable:

  trixium driver load      (or: sudo python3 -m software.driver load --dir software/kernel)

- Install them persistently (/lib/modules/.../extra, modules-load.d and a udev rule):

  make install

- Remove the drivers:

  sudo rmmod liteuart trixium

Secure Boot refuses unsigned modules ("Lockdown: insmod: unsigned module loading is
restricted"); disable it in the BIOS.
